      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a professional resume editor.\n\nCreate a concise targeted version of the candidate's original resume.\n\nORIGINAL RESUME:\n{{ $('Extract from File').item.json.text }}\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION:\n{{ $('Resume + JD').item.json.job_description }}\n\nRESUME IMPROVEMENT:\n{{ $json.text }}\n\nRULES:\n\nUse the original resume as the only source of truth.\n\nImprove wording and organization only when supported by the original resume.\n\nNever invent:\nskills\ntechnologies\ntools\nexperience\nresponsibilities\nprojects\ncertifications\nachievements\nmetrics\ndates\njob titles\nemployers\nleadership\nmanagement\ndeployment\nmonitoring\nproduction experience\nenterprise experience\nfeedback\ntesting\nstakeholder activities\n\nNever make a claim stronger than the original evidence.\n\nDo not add information merely because it appears in the job description.\n\nPreserve the original factual meaning.\n\nKeep the response SHORT.\n\nDo not rewrite information unnecessarily.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nDo not return Markdown.\nDo not return explanations.\nDo not return recommendation.\nDo not return interview questions.\nDo not return action plan.\nDo not return changes_made.\nDo not return content_not_added.\n\nUse exactly this structure:\n\n{\n  \"candidate_name\": \"\",\n  \"professional_summary\": \"\",\n  \"technical_skills\": [],\n  \"experience\": [],\n  \"projects\": [],\n  \"education\": [],\n  \"certifications\": [],\n  \"achievements\": [],\n  \"soft_skills\": []\n}\n\nUse the original resume information directly.\n\nKeep experience bullets concise.\n\nKeep project descriptions concise.\n\nDo not expand descriptions.\n\nDo not duplicate information.\n\nIMPORTANT JSON RULES:\n\nUse standard JSON only.\n\nUse double quotes.\n\nDo not escape underscores.\n\nDo not use backslashes before underscores.\n\nDo not use Markdown code fences.\n\nMake sure every array and object is closed.\n\nMake sure the response ends with the final closing brace:\n\n}\n\nReturn the COMPLETE JSON before finishing.",
